## Pattern: Scoped State Service + Interactive Islands

With per-page interactivity, the key insight is: **embed interactive components inside your static layout**. The layout itself stays static, but you place `@rendermode InteractiveServer` on individual components within it. All interactive components on a page share the same SignalR circuit, so a **scoped service** gives you per-user state that persists across enhanced navigations.

### Architecture

```
┌─ Static MainLayout ─────────────────────────┐
│  ┌─ <ThemeIndicator @rendermode="Server"/> ─┐│  ← interactive island
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────┘│
│  ┌─ @Body (page with @rendermode Server) ───┐│  ← interactive page
│  │   <ThemeToggle/>  <SettingsPanel/>        ││
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────┘│
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
         ↕ All share one circuit & scoped DI
```

### 1. The Service

```csharp
// Services/ThemeService.cs
public enum ThemeMode { Light, Dark, System }

public class ThemeService
{
    public ThemeMode Theme { get; private set; } = ThemeMode.System;
    public string AccentColor { get; private set; } = "#0078d4";

    public event Action? OnChange;

    public void SetTheme(ThemeMode theme)
    {
        Theme = theme;
        OnChange?.Invoke();
    }

    public void SetAccentColor(string color)
    {
        AccentColor = color;
        OnChange?.Invoke();
    }
}
```

Register as **scoped** (one instance per circuit):

```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<ThemeService>();
```

### 2. Consuming Components Subscribe to `OnChange`

```razor
@* Components/ThemeIndicator.razor *@
@implements IDisposable
@inject ThemeService Theme

<span style="color:@Theme.AccentColor">@Theme.Theme</span>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized() => Theme.OnChange += StateHasChanged;
    public void Dispose() => Theme.OnChange -= StateHasChanged;
}
```

### 3. Place Interactive Islands in Static Layout

```razor
@* MainLayout.razor — no @rendermode here *@
<header>
    <ThemeIndicator @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
</header>
<main>@Body</main>
```

### 4. Settings Page Mutates the Same Instance

```razor
@* Pages/Settings.razor *@
@page "/settings"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inject ThemeService Theme
@implements IDisposable

<select @bind="selectedTheme" @bind:after="ApplyTheme">
    @foreach (var t in Enum.GetValues<ThemeMode>())
    { <option value="@t">@t</option> }
</select>

<input type="color" @bind="accentColor" @bind:after="ApplyAccent" />

@code {
    ThemeMode selectedTheme;
    string accentColor = "";

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        selectedTheme = Theme.Theme;
        accentColor = Theme.AccentColor;
        Theme.OnChange += StateHasChanged;
    }

    void ApplyTheme() => Theme.SetTheme(selectedTheme);
    void ApplyAccent() => Theme.SetAccentColor(accentColor);
    public void Dispose() => Theme.OnChange -= StateHasChanged;
}
```

### Why This Works for Each Requirement

| # | Requirement | How |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Any component reads/writes | Scoped DI injection everywhere |
| 2 | Immediate cross-component update | `OnChange` event → `StateHasChanged` |
| 3 | Settings page updates header | Same scoped instance, same event |
| 4 | Per-user isolation | Scoped = per circuit = per user |
| 5 | Persists across navigation | Enhanced nav keeps the circuit alive |

The critical detail: **scoped services in Interactive Server mode live for the lifetime of the circuit**, and enhanced navigation reuses the circuit. No need for `CascadingValue`, no singleton pollution, no custom synchronization.
